Original compute logical Wave64 lane lowering
-------------------------------------------
This original PentaX implementation uses AMD's documented X-fast work-item
packing and Vulkan's linear local invocation index. AMD's OpenCL Programming
Optimization Guide, section 2.6.3.3 (page 2-21), describes successive work-items
in X-major order and packing them into 64-work-item waves:
https://www.amd.com/content/dam/amd/en/documents/radeon-tech-docs/programmer-references/AMD_OpenCL_Programming_Optimization_Guide2.pdf
The AMD RDNA2 ISA reference, section 2.1, describes the two halves and the
64-bit execution mask of Wave64:
https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/rdna2-shader-instruction-set-architecture
Khronos specifies the exact X-major LocalInvocationIndex formula:
https://docs.vulkan.org/refpages/latest/refpages/source/LocalInvocationIndex.html
The mapping is limited to independent lane identity and EXEC-bit selection;
native ballots and other cross-lane operations retain their existing exact
subgroup contract. No specification prose or third-party shader/test data was
copied into this implementation or its original tests.


